## Context
~/CNRS/code/ThinkTanksSurveyor is not a git repository (git reports none up to the /home mount point). It has both pyproject.toml and requirements.txt, no uv.lock, and `pip install` in its Makefile or README. Observed 2026-10-23.

Practice to reach: `rules/coding-python.md` (Environment principles and rules), tracked by 1206.

## Constraints
First decide whether it should be a repository; the practice's branch-and-PR flow assumes one. If it stays unversioned, align it in place and say so in the log.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] pyproject.toml and a committed uv.lock describe the dependencies; no hand-kept requirements.txt
- [ ] the Makefile has no PYTHON variable; recipes that run Python tools go through the `RUN` prefix
- [ ] no `pip install` in the Makefile or README
- [ ] the repo's own tests or smoke command pass from a bare shell, output quoted in the PR or log
- [ ] the alignment check of 1206 prints `ok` in ~/CNRS/code/ThinkTanksSurveyor
